    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and real-world logic—something I’ve always found fascinating but intimidating due to its precision. As someone who enjoys problem-solving in biology, it’s both a tool and a challenge; I appreciate its structure but sometimes struggle with the complexity of proofs or advanced concepts. My openness score suggests curiosity, so I’d rather tackle it step-by-step than avoid it entirely.",
